                <pb facs="0443" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg349"/>

                <head>No. 257.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr. Vignaud</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 3,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 252.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    instruction No. 218, of the 30th of April, relative to the application for the
                    discharge of Jean Pierre Arbios from the French army, I have to request you to
                    report as to the present condition of the case.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jas. D. Porter</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
